Extract data from the document into a JSON array of dictionaries representing flat table rows. Do not infer unstated data; use "NA" if missing.
​Extraction Rules:
​Company Name: Primary company explicitly mentioned.
​CIN: Extract the 21-digit alphanumeric code; otherwise "NA".
​Account Location: Account market/location; otherwise "NA".
​Account Number: Extract all. If "all accounts" is stated, return "All accounts". (CRITICAL: Create a separate dictionary for EACH account number).
​Account Currency: Mentioned currency (e.g., HKD, USD); otherwise "NA". Map to specific accounts if applicable.
​Effective Date: Stated effective date, or fallback to meeting/resolution date.
​Expiry Date: Written expiry date or exact terms (e.g., "Until further notice").
​Formatting Rule: For companies with multiple accounts, duplicate the shared fields (Company, CIN, Location, Dates) across every dictionary row for that company.
​Output Format:
[
  {
    "Company Name": "",
    "CIN": "",
    "Account Location": "",
    "Account Number": "", 
    "Account Currency": "",
    "Effective Date": "",
    "Expiry Date": ""
  }
]
